INSTALLATION
============

pythondialog 3.7.0 requires Python 3.10 or later and the dialog(1)
program (or a mostly-compatible replacement such as Xdialog).


Installing with pip
-------------------

From a clone of this repository, run one of:

  python3 -m pip install .
  python3 -m pip install -e .        # editable install for development

When doing so, make sure the pip executable belongs to the Python 3
installation you want to install pythondialog for. Inside a virtual
environment created with python -m venv this is always the case.


Installing on Gentoo
--------------------

A self-contained Portage overlay is provided in the gentoo/ directory.
See gentoo/README.md for the repositories.conf snippet and the emerge
command. The ebuild uses the modern PEP 517 build backend and installs
the module for all enabled Python implementations.


Building a source distribution
------------------------------

A PEP 517/621 source distribution can be built without third-party
tools:

  python3 -c "import setuptools.build_meta as b; print(b.build_sdist('dist'))"

or simply:

  make sdist

The resulting archive is written to dist/.


Running the tests
-----------------

  python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v

or:

  make test


Uninstallation
--------------

If installed with pip:

  python3 -m pip uninstall pythondialog

On Gentoo, use:

  emerge --unmerge dev-python/pythondialog
